-- Render lights
--
-- TODO OPT
--   We appear to be hitting an iteration/access limit. For
--   a 17x17 grid of boxes, we're looking at a total of 289
--   boxes. But with 250 lights on screen, that becomes 72,250
--   iterations and 72,250 bounds checks. It works out to about
--   18ns per iter or 1.3ms per frame.
--
--   At 144hz that's 19% of our frame budget. Rendering the
--   occluders themselves takes about the same amount of time,
--   another 19%. The rest of the light accumulation step takes
--   twice that, eating up 77% of our budget on shadow projection.
--
--   Obviously, we're not likely to have 250 lights onscreen. Though
--   currently we don't have a method to efficiently lookup entities
--   spatially and will have to iterate all occluders to gather or
--   exclude them. Additionally it presents a clear limit to the
--   number of iterations we can complete in a frame, including with
--   updates. We should investigate performance improvements with the ECS.
--   
--   Rendering Improvements
--     - Spatial Lookup Grid
--
--   ECS Improvements
--     - (?) Queries prefetch columns and index them sequentially
--     - (?) Queries should have a fast random or filtered lookup   
--         - This is to work in tandem with the spatial lookup grid
--   
-- Performance Budget
--    - 13ms Target Frametime (83.33ms)
--        - 60fps target, 20% variance buffer
--            - 75fps Effective Target
--            - ~13ms Frame Time
--        - Breakdown Targets
--            - 8ms Render (62%)
--            - 5ms Update (38%)
--    - 6GB RAM Target
--        - Most systems have at least 8GB of ram (40% have 16GB, Steam Hardware Survey)
--        - Assume OS uses ~2GB
--    - 4GB VRAM Target
--        - Most systems have at least 6GB of vram
--            - 40% have 8GB, Steam Hardware Survey
--            - NV RTX2060 has 6GB
--            - AMD RX6600 has 8GB
--        - Assume OS uses ~2GB (windows)
--    - Screen Resolution 4k (3840 x 2160)
--        -  720p - 3.0x Supersampling
--        - 1080p - 2.0x Supersampling
--        - 1440p - 1.5x Supersampling
--        - 2160p - Native
--             - 4k Users likely to have higher than target specs
--    - CPU Assumption
--        - 6 Threads (8 thread machine, assume 2 being used by system)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------